{
  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates skewness of lotteries, specifically preferring a lottery that is more left-skewed — meaning a greater probability is assigned to favorable outcomes compared to unfavorable ones. In this decision problem, Lottery A offers 2000 Euros with 100% probability, so it has no risk and is symmetric in outcome (only one outcome). Lottery B offers either +3000 Euros or -3000 Euros with 50% probability each, making it symmetric around zero. Since both outcomes are equally likely, Lottery B is symmetric (neither left-skewed nor right-skewed). Lottery A, with a single positive outcome and no negative outcome, has a favorable outcome with 100% probability, meaning it is left-skewed (all probability mass on the favorable side). Thus, the decision reason can be applied: Lottery A is more left-skewed than Lottery B, and the reason would prefer Lottery A.",
